{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1795543745,"nonce":"SqJQLcqza+qZDkqw0umh/pa0AQo=","target":"3048f2a8ce6fd90ddd458a02eddf2cd94fa7b5224f674d6a7d395bb8e59de35f","message":"A Neumann or Robin condition `ur.d(nr) - g` with `g = jno.np.parameter((n_nodes,))` solved correctly when `g` carried its value (module swap). Passing the value as `extra_params` (the traced route `jno.fvm` and a coupling use) gave NaN with `linear=jno.solve.lu()` and a diverging BiCGStab with the default. The flux rows read the injected value correctly (checked at `u = 0`), which hid the real fault.\n\n**Cause.** A data field is read as `(N, 1)` in the strong form, and `_referenced_models` shapes its stored value so. `_params_scope` laid the injected modules on top as they came, `(N,)`. In the row `grad(u).n - g` the `(N, 1)` gradient part minus an `(N,)` `g` broadcast to `(N, N)`: the row kept `g` and lost its gradient, the right-edge Jacobian rows were zero apart from the corners, and the system was singular (cond 5e17).\n\n**Reproduce.** `tests/test_fdm.py::test_a_neumann_flux_injected_as_traced_data_gives_the_linear_solution_and_its_gradient`: `-Δu = 0`, `u = 1` on the left, `∂u/∂n = g` injected on the right, insulated top and bottom, so `u = 1 + g·x`.\n\n**Fix.** Commit b91fcb30 in #345. `jno/_strong_form.py` sends every module of the scope, stored or injected, through one rule (`_nodal_module`), so a value evaluates the same whichever route it takes. The same commit fixes a second fault: the march read a Dirichlet value that is a nodal data field from its stored value and ignored the injected one (`_override`, how a coupling window passes its data). It now reads it through `_eval_value` with the injected scope (`jno/fdm.py`). Guards: the test above (closed form to 1e-10 under `jax.jit` with `lu`, and `d(mean right-edge u)/d(uniform g) = 1`) and `tests/test_fdm.py::test_a_dirichlet_value_injected_as_data_holds_in_a_march` (every saved state holds the injected 2 on the left; it was 0).\n\n**Note.** The fdm march itself was not yet jit-safe with traced data at that commit (a structural probe converts a tracer). Until then fdm participants in a coupling used the stored-value route.","files":null}]}